{"title":"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Aleksander Ivanov, Bulgaria</i>)\nDetermine all pairs of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/0109673cc9e48c41e3620d26b37e9cf4e8c014d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^2}{2ab^2-b^3+1}\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"40\" />\nis a positive integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The only solutions are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb2b1ea15e2c9246b73f109181b3b4d829d57368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b) = (2n,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3decae047ec6c48905c42262cfbcdc59451e819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b) = (n,2n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/6285ec5427c1d120bd5108c71c56a8f57c0f7d6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8n^4-n,2n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"19\" /> for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>First, we note that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf590e9abb33aa9776ddc386b1ba6ee7b43fa413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, the given expression is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf6922a5a592ac6c1094e79bc83a79ce12cf0fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />, which is an integer if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is even.\n</p><p>Now, suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is a solution not of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd0da90a2dc51e20f535776d4f779a7c730edb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.  We have already given all solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf590e9abb33aa9776ddc386b1ba6ee7b43fa413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />; then for this new solution, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/40920163c12ad9f3ce69942d9b625b88ac82923f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.  Let us denote\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5ec3c2fd5dafcb8d8d0ee69cbc7a6482f35d2a2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^2}{2ab^2-b^3+1} = k .\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"40\" />\nDenote\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e892410c449c8a83bfd779ae05f8e37814ec8f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(t) = t^2 - 2kb^2 t + k(b^3-1) .\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"19\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45cf3d27e8df8783a5deab3ea85d1d1aff2ecd28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(b^3-1) &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, there must be some other root <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1e51ef5511c6d27c703b84edc8ff93ffbc3717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;$\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531b19153fc571e579244df5c6b270dd960f92be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39; \\ge a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b57b3ee776ca19e694837e6651ee352627a373.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 \\le aa&#39; = k(b^3-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/5506bbddc68d7c5faf06fcd2fef0367ecf298aa6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = \\frac{a^2}{2ab^2-b^3+1} \\le k \\frac{b^3-1}{2ab^2-b^3+1},\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"40\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e71febf2efde918f515e0c9db1b569da1b406f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2ab^2 - (b^3-1) \\le b^3-1,\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"19\" />\nwhich reduces to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/2/1a2b5516433a7c3f30786e05c68e3700377ed0c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a \\le b - \\frac{1}{b^2} &lt; b .\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"37\" />\nIt follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9f6f448332b2d8b10f37f822900e1e2e655b78e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 &lt; 2ab^2 -b^3 + 1 \\le a^2 &lt; b^2 ,\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba1242604e8889e5542af61c3d97255bccd40d65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 &lt; (2a-b)b^2 + 1 &lt; b^2 .\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are integers, this can only happen when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e6d76609e507d60b3cf5bd56e9f43250cdeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a-b=0$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa86b0ef48a28317d10a53f409f74d756ae49fd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,2n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29e2c9b2daf9650c488f5637ff69a8489fa4bf70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = n^2$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.  It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f03305465d1342b966a1e12dd161b1b6021c5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a&#39; = \\frac{k(b^3-1)}{a} = 8n^4-n.\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"39\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1e51ef5511c6d27c703b84edc8ff93ffbc3717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;$\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> is the other root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92bb389b4a381784023b3820b41a68e78d0be763.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a&#39;,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> also satisfies the problem's condition.  Therefore the solutions are exactly the ones given at the solution's start.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO\" title=\"2003 IMO\">2003 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;Forum/viewtopic.php?p=262#262 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202445\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 225/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6684/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.612      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.612      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6814:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202445 and revision id 258111. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}